  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 117 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nIt's shaping up to be a beautiful day for shopping on Black Friday, \nwith highs in the mid to upper 60s across much of the region, with \nthe river valleys seeing 70s. Prevailing westerly winds at around 10-\n15 mph will enhance the warming trend we see going into the weekend. \nLows Friday night into Saturday also trend upwards, but remain \nchilly with lows in the low to mid 40s across the area and close to \n50F in the Presidio Valley and Big Bend Area. On Saturday, lee \ntroughing moves across the region from the west, reinforcing the \nwarming trend Saturday and bringing gusty (25-35 mph) winds with \nlocally faster in the higher terrain (near 50 mph). Behind the lee \ntroughing, a Pacific front moves through late Saturday and Sunday \nmorning bringing cool temperatures, with highs in the mid to upper \n50s across much the area and mid to upper 60s in the Presidio Valley \nand Big Bend Area. Low temperatures Sunday night and Monday morning \nwill decline to mid 30s and 40s across the area. Light winds are \nforecast to return Sunday. Temperatures rebound quickly Monday with \nhighs reaching the mid 60s to 70s and lows in the mid 40s and 50s, \nwhere they are expected to remain through early next week. Light \nwesterly winds are forecast to prevail through early next week.\n\nBynum",
